# Same bytes on every OS: text is stored and checked out with LF line endings, whatever each
# developer's core.autocrlf says. Shell scripts with CRLF break on macOS/Linux and in containers;
# Windows tools (PowerShell, VS Code, Docker, Python, Node) all read LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch line endings or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
